-- Trace data foundation v2.22.0: Phase 4 transition-planning content (D27 pm-bridges-v1, D28 pm-actions-v1, D29 pm-eligibility-v1).
-- GENERATED by scripts/build_transition_content.py from the reviewed JSON files. Do not edit by hand; edit the JSON
-- and regenerate.
-- D27: A small, target-specific catalogue. A bridge role is a candidate route, never a default: it is recommended only when it closes the user's material gaps, its responsibilities develop them, the user has a credible way in, the direct route is less supported, and it leads to the target. Program Manager is deliberately not a bridge (D27). Responsibilities are paraphrased from the sources; 'develops' and entry signals are Trace's curated reading of those responsibilities against the pm-v1.1 requirements.
-- D28: Templates are instantiated per requirement from the user's own assessment: Gap -> Build (stage 1) and Demonstrate (stage 2); Transferable -> Demonstrate (stage 2) and Reposition (stage 3); Demonstrated -> Reposition (stage 3) only; Unknown -> resolve the missing information first (stage 0), no capability action. Stage 4 is always considered. No courses, providers, costs, timelines, placement outcomes or job openings are named or implied; current openings come only from verified postings in the knowledge base.
-- D29: Structure preserves AND (all) / OR (any), ranges and required versus preferred. Leaves: years_in_families (reviewed roles in the named role families, from partial dates: 'meets' only when the certain minimum reaches the stated minimum, 'does not meet' only when the possible maximum cannot), product_exposure (confirmed, categorised responsibility evidence in a role of the named families showing a product-ownership area; a job title alone never counts), current_role_in_families and not_transitioning_from (the user's CURRENT confirmed role only; earlier roles never trigger an exclusion), total_years, qualification (an 'or equivalent' clause never gives 'does not meet'; a missing qualification record is unclear, never absence), and stated_condition (a condition the profile cannot show, such as a product domain; always unclear). Preferred criteria are reported but never decide the outcome.
-- Curated public reference content: no user data, no synthetic test data.

